  "live_records": {
    "q-53161": {
      "dom_id": "step-q53161",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14212968/assets/0640883625711f20e1441946461abd0f352ed1418065b325f48ea2b709fef230.png)\n\nA cableway system is descending at an angle of ${45}^{∘},$ and the speed of its cabin $C$ is $10\\,\\text{mi/h}.$ The cabin casts a shadow $S$ vertically downwards to the ground. Assuming the angle of elevation doesn't change, find the rate at which the distance between the cableway's shadow to the landing point $L$ is decreasing.",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14212968/assets/4d2a9ab6bc60aa5733be4dc29aea2b03d16edbebed371963b795297a4c79a676.png)\n\nLet $x$ be the distance from the cableway's shadow to the landing point, and let $z$ be the distance between the landing point and the cabin, as shown above.\n\nWe want to find $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$ To do this, let's start by setting up a relation between $x$ and $z.$ Relative to the angle $\\theta ={45}^{∘},$ the sides $x$ and $z$ are the adjacent and hypotenuse, respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({45}^{∘}) & =\\frac{x}{z} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{x}{z} \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate both sides of the equation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}z) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that $\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}=-10\\,\\text{mi/h}$ (negative because the distance between the cableway's shadow and the landing point is decreasing). Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot (-10)=-5\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the horizontal distance is decreasing at a rate of $5\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{mi/h}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
